SWEET page flip (patch 0162, boot-arg sweetflip=2, default off; docs/research/44 sections 2 and 5): the screen-sized surfaces backboardd presents live in a scanout carve-out below 4 GB (16 slots of 16 MiB from 0xC8000000, write-combined only) and AppleCLCD::present() points the display at them (RDMA L0 SRC_SIZE / SRC_OFFSET / BASEADDR_Y8 + window 5 update request) instead of copying 10 MB with the CPU each frame. Run flip1-oriole3 proved the display scans physical addresses (photo of the test buffer). Any other frame (more layers, an ordinary surface, a partial rectangle, blanking) goes back to the boot framebuffer and the copy.
SweetSurface: sweet_carve_wanted (sweetflip=2, backboardd, 4 bytes per pixel, at least 1080x2400, fits a slot), slot bitmap, carveSlot/carvePhys, slot given back in free(). Mali: imports carve-out surfaces, sweet_mali_map accepts carve-out pages although pmap_valid_page() does not, and neither it nor boCacheSync flushes them (they are never mapped cacheable; phystokv() has no address for them). The display state is checked once against run dpu2's before the first flip.

